-e11e-4fef-b564-9c6f9356ce91" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="70">Excellent — that’s a common issue, and I can help you fix it easily.</p>
<p data-start="72" data-end="215">When you see <strong data-start="85" data-end="121">“youtube.com refused to connect”</strong> inside your <code data-start="134" data-end="144">&lt;iframe&gt;</code>, it means the <strong data-start="159" data-end="172">embed URL</strong> is incorrect.<br data-start="186" data-end="189">
Let’s fix it properly 👇</p>
<hr data-start="217" data-end="220">
<h2 data-start="222" data-end="270">✅ 1. The Correct Way to Embed a YouTube Video</h2>
<p data-start="272" data-end="357">Make sure your <code data-start="287" data-end="297">&lt;iframe&gt;</code> uses the <strong data-start="307" data-end="321">embed link</strong>, not the normal YouTube watch link.</p>
